From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Dutton <chris@bigcove.io>
Date: Mon, 1 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Always advertise NL80211_IFTYPE_AP

Upstream gates the AP interface type behind CONFIG_AP_MODE, which the
host/Makefile only defines when CONFIG_AP_SUPPORT=y is passed on the make
command line. Buildroot's kernel-module infrastructure does not feed that
variable into the Kbuild compile, so -DCONFIG_AP_MODE is never set and
wlan0 comes up advertising only NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION -- wpa_supplicant
mode=2 (SoftAP) then has no AP iftype to use and no beacon is sent.

The AP cfg80211 ops (start_ap/change_beacon/stop_ap/...) are always
compiled regardless of CONFIG_AP_MODE; only this interface_modes line is
guarded. Advertise AP unconditionally so SoftAP works without relying on
the make-time define.

Signed-off-by: Chris Dutton <chris@bigcove.io>
---
--- a/esp_hosted_ng/host/esp_cfg80211.c
+++ b/esp_hosted_ng/host/esp_cfg80211.c
@@ -1204,10 +1204,8 @@

 	set_wiphy_dev(wiphy, esp_dev->dev);

-	wiphy->interface_modes = BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION);
-#ifdef CONFIG_AP_MODE
-	wiphy->interface_modes |= BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP);
-#endif
+	wiphy->interface_modes = BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION) |
+				 BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP);
 	wiphy->bands[NL80211_BAND_2GHZ] = &esp_wifi_bands_2ghz;
 	if (adapter->chipset == ESP_FIRMWARE_CHIP_ESP32C5) {
 		wiphy->bands[NL80211_BAND_5GHZ] = &esp_wifi_bands_5ghz;
--
